# DECLARED COUNT of occurrences of a pwg-branded ontology namespace.
# See scripts/verify_no_foreign_ontology_namespace.sh for why this exists.
#
# THE BASIS OF THIS NUMBER CHANGED on 2026-08-17, and saying so is the whole
# point of this comment. It previously counted the unregistered domain only,
# and read 276. It now counts BOTH pwg-branded domains, because the second is
# a namespace the old regex could not see and a migration would have left
# behind:
#
#     unregistered domain   276   NXDOMAIN from two networks
#     mDNS-reserved domain   15   CM019 enrichment writes enriched preferences here
#     ---------------------------
#     total                 291   across 66 files
#
# A ratchet number that silently changes basis is not evidence about anything,
# so the rise from 276 is a WIDER MEASUREMENT, not a regression. Comparing it
# to the old 276 compares two different questions.
#
# The gate excludes its own script, this file, and its own test from the scan:
# all three NAME the domains in prose to explain themselves, and an instrument
# that counts its own documentation moves when you edit a comment.
#
# 🔴 THE FIRST VERSION OF THAT EXCLUSION DID NOT WORK, AND THE NUMBER HERE
# CARRIED THE ERROR. The pathspec read `tests/test_no_...` while the file is at
# `scripts/tests/test_no_...`, so the test fixture was never excluded and its
# one occurrence was counted as a shipping occurrence: declared 292 where the
# tree holds 291. The comment asserted an exclusion the code did not perform,
# which is the same instrument-and-defect-on-different-surfaces shape this gate
# exists to catch, one level in. Control 9 in the test suite now pins it: the
# reading must not move when the instrument's own prose changes.
#
# THIS NUMBER MAY ONLY GO DOWN FROM HERE. Lower it in the same commit that
# removes occurrences. It reaches 0 when the source repos are migrated and
# re-vendored, and then it stays at 0 forever.
291
